      "acceptance": {
        "criteria": [
          "Resource subclasses can be registered with Api.add_resource on Flask apps and Blueprints, including route parameters, endpoint names, URL prefixes, and url_for generation.",
          "Resource dispatch supports HTTP methods, HEAD/OPTIONS/405 behaviour, resource method decorators, global decorators, and return shapes of data, (data, status), and (data, status, headers).",
          "RequestParser and Argument parse parameters from json, args, form, values, headers, cookies, files, and view_args with conversion, defaults, required validation, choices, append action, operators, trimming, nullability, bundling, strict mode, parser copy/replace/remove, Namespace access, and store_m",
          "fields and marshal serialize strings, integers, floats, booleans, decimals, datetimes, URLs, nested objects, lists, raw values, formatted strings, attributes, callables, defaults, envelopes, and marshalling errors as documented.",
          "inputs validators convert and validate booleans, dates, positive/natural integers, integer ranges, regexes, URLs, RFC822/ISO8601 datetimes, and ISO8601 intervals including internal normalization helpers.",
          "Api content negotiation chooses representations using Accept headers, default_mediatype, q values, custom representation decorators, and produces JSON via RESTFUL_JSON configuration and debug pretty printing.",
          "abort and Api error handling produce documented error payloads, custom errors, 401 challenges, signal emission, Flask PROPAGATE_EXCEPTIONS-compatible propagation, API/non-API error routing, and catch_all_404s behaviour.",
          "utils.cors.crossdomain applies CORS and preflight headers according to origin, methods, headers, expose_headers, max_age, credentials, attach_to_all, and automatic_options.",
          "utils.crypto encrypt/decrypt round-trips Python data with AES-CBC using the frozen padding constants and validates key/seed sizes.",
          "Examples in examples/todo.py, examples/todo_simple.py, and examples/xml_representation.py are directly runnable modules using the public API.",
          "Sphinx documentation files and the docs FlaskyStyle theme support import/render configuration, and scripts/release.py exposes point_release."
        ],
        "corner_cases": [
          "Malformed numeric/date/URL/regex inputs raise clear ValueError or MarshallingException rather than silently returning incorrect data.",
          "None, missing values, empty lists, sets, indexable non-strings, dict attributes, object attributes, nested dot paths, callable attributes, and partial functions are handled in marshalling.",
          "Accept headers with q=0, wildcards, no matching mediatype, no default mediatype, and no representations return the documented response or not-acceptable behaviour.",
          "Request parsing must preserve case-sensitive and case-insensitive choice semantics, append multiple values from JSON and query strings, ignore conversion errors when requested, and bundle multiple failures when configured.",
          "Blueprint registration before and after Api initialization must preserve endpoint names and route prefixes.",
          "Import paths and constants frozen in the first milestone must not be removed, renamed, or moved.",
          "Crypto padding must round-trip byte data whose length is exactly a block size, one byte short of a block, empty, or contains null bytes.",
          "CORS must not attach headers when attach_to_all is false and the request is not an automatic OPTIONS response."
